================================================================================
## Stop tracking local planning trees on GitHub
================================================================================

Context: `.planning/`, `.superpowers/`, and `docs/superpowers/` were local
agent working drafts (SPECs, SDD reports, brainstorming specs) that had
already been committed. They do not belong on GitHub. Eval datasets that CI
needs already live under `tests/eval/datasets/`. Untrack the trees, gitignore
the whole `.planning/` directory, and retarget the AI-feature gate at the
committed eval artifacts.

Changes:

1. .gitignore
   Ignore the entire `.planning/` tree (SPECs, ROADMAP, PLAN.md stay local).
2. .github/workflows/eval-gate.yml
   Drop the SPEC.md-on-checkout job; keep dataset size + MLflow URI checks.
3. .cursor/12-ai-feature-lifecycle.mdc
   Gate on `tests/eval/datasets/<agent>/`; SPEC.md is local-only.
4. .cursor/07-project-conventions.mdc
   Document that planning trees are gitignored.
5. .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
   Stop requiring committed SPEC/PLAN paths.
6. .github/PR_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md
   Reviewer blocks on committed eval datasets, not `.planning/`.
7. docs/contributing.md
   Required PR artifacts are eval dataset + MLflow URI.
8. docs/README.md
   Superpowers/sphinx extras described as local, not linked as published docs.
9. tests/eval/test_staged_dataset_metadata_shape.py
   Stop requiring a `.planning/` mirror of the owl-generator dataset.
10. tests/eval/thresholds.yaml
    Note that SPEC.md is local.
11. .claude/skills/ai-feature/SKILL.md
    Dataset output is `tests/eval/datasets/` only.

